                                        <p class="mb-0 text-muted"><em>Result: You will see the JSON list of the 2 default books!</em></p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <!-- Test POST -->
                            <div class="accordion-item border-0 mb-3 rounded-3 overflow-hidden">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold bg-light" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#testPost">
                                        <i class="fas fa-upload text-success me-2"></i> 2. Test POST (Create Data)
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="testPost" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#swaggerAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Click on <strong>POST /api/books</strong> → <strong>Try it out</strong>. Paste this JSON:</p>
                                        <div class="modern-code-box py-3 mb-3" data-lang="JSON">
<pre class="mb-0"><code>{ "title": "C# in Depth", "author": "Jon Skeet" }</code></pre>
                                        </div>
                                        <p>Click <strong>Execute</strong>.</p>
                                        <p class="mb-0 text-muted"><em>Result: <code>201 Created</code>. The new book is added!</em></p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <!-- Test PUT -->
                            <div class="accordion-item border-0 mb-3 rounded-3 overflow-hidden">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold bg-light" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#testPut">
                                        <i class="fas fa-edit text-warning me-2"></i> 3. Test PUT (Update Data)
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="testPut" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#swaggerAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Click on <strong>PUT /api/books/1</strong> → <strong>Try it out</strong>. Paste this JSON to fix the author's name:</p>
                                        <div class="modern-code-box py-3 mb-3" data-lang="JSON">
<pre class="mb-0"><code>{ "id": 1, "title": "Clean Code", "author": "Robert C. Martin" }</code></pre>
                                        </div>
                                        <p>Click <strong>Execute</strong>.</p>
                                        <p class="mb-0 text-muted"><em>Result: <code>204 No Content</code>. The book was updated successfully!</em></p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <!-- Test DELETE -->
                            <div class="accordion-item border-0 rounded-3 overflow-hidden">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold bg-light" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#testDelete">
                                        <i class="fas fa-trash-alt text-danger me-2"></i> 4. Test DELETE (Remove Data)
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="testDelete" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#swaggerAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Click on <strong>DELETE /api/books/2</strong> → <strong>Try it out</strong> → <strong>Execute</strong>.</p>
                                        <p class="mb-0 text-muted"><em>Result: <code>204 No Content</code>. The book is deleted!</em></p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="alert alert-success border-0 mt-4 shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4">
                            <h4 class="alert-heading fw-bold"><i class="fas fa-trophy me-2"></i> Mastered!</h4>
                            <p class="mb-0 fs-5">You just built and tested a complete CRUD API. You used all 4 HTTP methods to Read, Create, Update, and Delete data from a real API.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- END OF LAB -->

